|---|---|---|
| `config/brand/sacred-ground-logo-long.png` | **21848** | Awnings, wide signs |
| `config/brand/sacred-ground-logo-stacked-white.png` | **21849** | Windows, stacked lockups |

WordPress: `Sacred-Ground-logo-3.png` (long) and `Sacred-Ground-logo-Stacked-white-1.png` (stacked). White SACRED GROUND + gold wave.

## How to put them on a plate

1. Pass `selectedImages: [21848, 21849]` on every new gen that shows a shop / awning / window.
2. Or leave the awning/window **blank** and **stamp** these PNGs after. Stamping is safer.
3. Circular sun (`sacred-ground-logo-circle-transparent.png`) stays the **corner mark** only — it does **not** replace the wordmark on awnings.

## Never

- Invent SACRED GROUND / Sacred Ground lettering (the model garbles it)
- Invent a new sun, stick-sun, or generic sans shop name
- Paint “white SACRED GROUND, blank between words, no swoosh” — that old line caused this. Use the real files. The real wordmark **has** the gold wave.

